AB  - ChatGPT has rapidly gained traction as a tool to address writing challenges across diverse academic contexts. This meta-analysis evaluates the effectiveness of ChatGPT in enhancing EFL Students' writing skills and explores seven moderator variables, educational level, control group, intervention duration, sampling method, application purpose, and data type, to assess their influence on writing outcomes. The results reveal a significant overall effect size (Hedges' g = 0.906, SE = 0.088, p < .001), highlighting ChatGPT's primary applications in writing instruction, assessment, and scoring, with the most pronounced benefits observed in instructional contexts. Additionally, ChatGPT significantly boosts EFL Students' writing self-efficacy by enhancing their confidence and fostering a supportive learning environment. These findings suggest that integrating ChatGPT into teaching practices can improve pedagogical strategies, stimulate student motivation, and establish an engaging writing atmosphere. The study underscores the potential of ChatGPT to advance technology-enhanced language learning and offers actionable insights for educators seeking to optimize its use in fostering students' writing development.
